    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Long before modern development, Kaneohe was the royal seat of early Hawaiian kings, a center of power on Oʻahu.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.britannica.com/place/Kaneohe"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Taro and sweet potatoes once thrived here, thanks to the region’s abundant rainfall and fertile volcanic soil.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/K%C4%81ne%CA%BBohe%2C_Hawaii"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The area once boasted 30 royal fishponds, showcasing sophisticated ancient aquaculture techniques.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/K%C4%81ne%CA%BBohe%2C_Hawaii"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Today, banana is the only crop that still reaches commercial scale in Kaneohe’s tropical climate.",
